r possibility  how to get  from a to b so what i did i took several  rows from a to b and different one  and also i tried to  not only to go from a to b but just from  c to d and  from home to work from some other places  and then i recorded all of them  and i tried to find some  rules uh or some  [Music]  way to identify which is the best way to  get  from a to b and then i  loaded i did plenty plenty plenty of  trips and just for this uh presentation  i just  tried just through the three of them and  i loaded them into uh joseen  and then tried to find all the  intersections  and all the points of interest so for  example we have here a crossroad  where there are some trips going from  between  different points and then not  automatically but manually i  found the points where of intersections  and then i defined a new um  network with a bath between these  spots and um then i saw that okay there  are also some  crossroads that are not only simple  crossroads where you can  turn left right to go straight ahead at  any time  there are also some crossroads with  traffic lights where you are not allowed  to turn  left where turning right is much faster  than going straight ahead  and this way i  built a whole network  there is a project in the python because  i wanted  to write a real project in  python on github which is called apigo  home  using a few third-party libraries for  geographical  and mathematical computing and  iplay flat and apple widgets are  libraries for  jupyter notebook representation  interactive  work with the data on a map  and then i took my all my  trips and then tried to find all the  intersections  and manually enter them  to the gpx files  at the end i had a network of  all the intersections and all the roots  these are not based  on the map so it doesn't use any map  information it uses only  the data from my gps tracker  and then for example here to get from a  to i  there is one root there is another  possible root  and there was a third root but you see  that for example between a and b  that i have already two data and this is  exactly what makes it individual because  if i go on right on the segment  between two intersections uh it depends  on my speed on my acceleration braking  on my behavior  or in front of obstacles uh on the  currently weather on the current traffic  uh current route condition um  that when i take some segments several  times or many times  i will get a lot of data um a lot of  time data like  this number of seconds uh passed between  points and a b and i will get some  mathematical  this distribution or mathematical  representation  of how fast can i get from a to b and  then composing it uh to a bigger network  how to get between any two points  because then  i could take a trip for example from g  to c and then  you see that probably the fastest route  maybe  a b e f i although i have never taken  exactly this route so this is manhattan  distance that i'm compiling  using much more data that i would have  only if traveling between a and b  then with this data i could build some  statistical representation  so for example if i go if i have a  segment that goes  through the city uh and there is a  traffic light so it can take somewhere  between four and eight minutes depending  on the traffic light  and there is another way around through  a park  which is in the average is a little bit  slower but  uh there are no lights so actually i  will always  need around six seven minutes uh and in  this case if  i statistically try to try to find the  best  route i can say oh i am feeling lucky so  it's sunday morning nice weather nobody  is there  so i will be actually in average will be  faster than the average  uh in this case the route through the  city will be faster  but if i want to make sure and i want to  get uh somewhere  and make sure that i won't need more  than a certain amount of time i will  try to see in the upper limits  of the distribution and in this case i  see that going  through around through the park is  actually  faster than going through the city so  this is how it looks like you can go  to buy go home download it try it with  your own data  or there is a mybinder link or  button where you can click and it will  load and then you can upload your gpx  data  and test them and then choose  some two points in your surroundings and  in the quantile you ask zero is the  fastest uh  one is the slowest the safest one and  then it will  tell you how far how much time you need  it so for example in this case  uh between the castle and the park  i needed uh nine minutes and 11 seconds  in the fastest case but the slowest  with all the lights and traffic and  everything took me 22 minutes  on the other hand if i ask for the  safest route it will give me this one  because the fastest time was actually 11  43 which is a little bit more but i was  never slower than 13 minutes and 18  seconds  there are plenty of things that i would  like to work on  if i go home um i would be happy to hear  your feedback  so there is something like isochrone map  i have a point and i want to know  in which area i can get within 5 10 or  15 minutes  it should automatically detect the gps  problems uh detect brakes and vehicle  swept so for example if i just  get off the bicycle and push for a while  they take that edit intersections  automatically because now i do it  everything manually maybe some machine  learning depending on  which is which weekday or day time is it  integrate with openstreetmap with the  data from the map  avoid and prefer tracks and maybe do it  everything in postgresql without using  python at  all and maybe up app or some more  platforms  i would like to hear from you thank you  very much

